---
import Base from '../../../layouts/Base.astro';
import EmailCapture from '../../../components/EmailCapture.astro';
import AccGroup from '../../../components/AccGroup.astro';
import RelatedEquipment from '../../../components/RelatedEquipment.astro';
import ModelStatus from '../../../components/ModelStatus.astro';
import { XDJ_AZ, REKORDBOX } from '../../../data/facts.js';

/**
 * XDJ-AZ, the four channel all-in-one and the fourth equipment kind on this
 * site. Structure, section order and the style block match the other Pioneer
 * model pages so the hardware pages stay one family. Every version number, file
 * system and source link is rendered from XDJ_AZ in facts.js.
 *
 * WHAT LEADS THE PAGE, and why in this order.
 *
 * 1. THE LIBRARY TRAP. This unit reads OneLibrary only. A USB exported the old
 *    way carries no library it can read, so the screen reports the database was
 *    not found and nothing loads. It is the single most likely way a prepared
 *    DJ arrives and cannot play, and the fix is a rekordbox export setting.
 *
 * 2. NO AUDIO, BLACKOUTS, FREEZES. An internal component defect in certain early
 *    units caused exactly that, and firmware 1.05 addresses the same symptom
 *    set. On a unit that is the whole booth, any of the three takes the room
 *    down at once, so it leads the emergency section. The hardware side has a
 *    free inspection and repair programme, and AlphaTheta published no serial
 *    range, so the honest instruction is to contact support rather than guess.
 *
 * 3. FILE SYSTEMS. FAT, FAT32, exFAT and HFS+, never NTFS, and exFAT is the one
 *    a DJ coming from older gear does not expect to have.
 *
 * This is an AlphaTheta unit, so firmware, storage, library and rekordbox are
 * its real subjects and the page treats them as such.
 */
const UPDATED = XDJ_AZ.checked;
const FLOOR = XDJ_AZ.newestKnown;
const FS = XDJ_AZ.fileSystems.join(', ');

const schema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'TechArticle',
  '@id': 'https://www.savemygig.com/knowledge/pioneer-dj/xdj-az#article',
  headline: 'XDJ-AZ: the operational reference',
  description: `What every DJ should know before working an XDJ-AZ: it reads OneLibrary only so an old USB export will not load, it reads ${FS} but never NTFS, and the audio, blackout and freeze fault fixed in firmware ${XDJ_AZ.audioBlackoutFreezeFix}.`,
  author: { '@id': 'https://www.savemygig.com/#org' },
  publisher: { '@id': 'https://www.savemygig.com/#org' },
  datePublished: '2026-08-08',
  dateModified: '2026-08-08',
  inLanguage: 'en',
  mainEntityOfPage: { '@id': 'https://www.savemygig.com/knowledge/pioneer-dj/xdj-az#webpage' },
  image: 'https://www.savemygig.com/images/xdj-az-panel-full.webp',
};
---
<Base
  title="XDJ-AZ: OneLibrary, exFAT, the Audio Fix | Save My Gig"
  description="The XDJ-AZ field manual: why an old USB export will not load, the file systems it reads, and the audio, blackout and freeze fault and its fix."
  path="/knowledge/pioneer-dj/xdj-az"
  crumbName="XDJ-AZ"
>
  <script type="application/ld+json" slot="head" set:html={JSON.stringify(schema)} />

  <main class="wrap wrap-wide">
    <nav class="crumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/knowledge">Knowledge base</a> <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <a href="/knowledge/pioneer-dj">Pioneer DJ / AlphaTheta</a> <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <span>XDJ-AZ</span>
    </nav>

    <div class="hw-head">
      <div class="hw-head-text">
        <ModelStatus slug="xdj-az" checked={UPDATED} />
        <h1 class="rb-h1">XDJ-AZ, <span class="accent">the field manual</span></h1>
      </div>
      <a
        class="hw-thumb"
        href="#xdj-az-lightbox"
        aria-label="Open a larger photo of the XDJ-AZ control surface"
      >
        <img
          src="/images/xdj-az-panel-thumb.webp"
          alt="Pioneer DJ AlphaTheta XDJ-AZ all-in-one DJ system, top view"
          width="887"
          height="500"
          loading="lazy"
        />
      </a>
    </div>

    <div class="lightbox" id="xdj-az-lightbox">
      <a href="#" class="lightbox-backdrop" aria-label="Close"></a>
      <a href="#" class="lightbox-close" aria-label="Close">&times;</a>
      <img
        src="/images/xdj-az-panel-full.webp"
        srcset="/images/xdj-az-panel-800.webp 800w, /images/xdj-az-panel-full.webp 1400w"
        sizes="92vw"
        alt="Pioneer DJ AlphaTheta XDJ-AZ all-in-one DJ system, top view"
        width="1400"
        height="789"
        loading="lazy"
      />
    </div>

    <div class="panel panel-go">
      <input type="checkbox" id="sv-toggle" class="sv-toggle sr-only" />
      <p class="sv-text" style="margin:0">
        <strong>Booth briefing.</strong> A four channel all-in-one, so a fault
        takes the whole booth down at once rather than one deck. It reads
        <strong>OneLibrary only</strong>: a USB exported the old way loads
        nothing and the screen reports the database was not found, so export from
        rekordbox {REKORDBOX.dualFormatFloor} or later, which writes both formats. File systems are
        <strong>{FS}</strong>, never NTFS. If an early unit drops audio, blacks
        out or freezes, that is a documented defect with a free repair, and
        firmware {XDJ_AZ.audioBlackoutFreezeFix} addresses the same symptoms.
        Highest published version is <strong>{FLOOR}</strong>.
      </p>
      <label for="sv-toggle" class="sv-more">Read more…</label>
      <label for="sv-toggle" class="sv-more sv-more-open">Read less</label>
    </div>

    <AccGroup icon="zap" title="Emergency fixes" />

    <details class="acc-sec" name="xdjaz-acc" id="database-not-found">
      <summary><h3 class="acc-h2">The USB will not load and the screen says the database was not found</h3><span class="acc-chev" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
      <div class="acc-body">
        <p><strong>Short answer.</strong> The drive was exported the old way. The
        XDJ-AZ reads <strong>OneLibrary</strong> only, and a USB carrying only the
        older Device Library has nothing on it this unit can read, so it reports
        the rekordbox database as not found. Re-export the drive from rekordbox {REKORDBOX.dualFormatFloor} or later, which writes both library formats at once.</p>
        <p><strong>Why this happens.</strong> AlphaTheta moved this unit and the
        others in its generation to OneLibrary, while most players in circulation
        still read the original Device Library. A drive built for an older player
        is not corrupt and the AZ is not faulty, they are two library formats and
        this unit reads only the newer one.</p>
        <p><strong>Fix it now.</strong> If you have a laptop with a current
        rekordbox, re-export the drive and both formats are written, so the same
        stick then works here and on an older CDJ. With no laptop in the booth,
        the fastest route is a drive somebody else already exported from a recent
        rekordbox, or playing from a linked player over PRO DJ LINK.</p>
        <p><strong>Avoid it next time.</strong> Export from rekordbox {REKORDBOX.dualFormatFloor} or later as a habit, not just for this gig. One drive written that way plays
        on the OneLibrary units and on the Device Library units, which is the
        whole point of the change, and it removes the guesswork about which venue
        has which generation.</p>
        <p class="acc-related">Related: <a href="#file-systems">The file systems it reads</a> <a href="/fix/playlists-not-showing-cdj">Playlists not showing</a> <a href="/knowledge/pioneer-dj/rekordbox#onelibrary">OneLibrary vs Device Library</a></p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="acc-sec" name="xdjaz-acc" id="no-audio">
      <summary><h3 class="acc-h2">No audio, the screen blacks out, or the unit freezes</h3><span class="acc-chev" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
      <div class="acc-body">
        <p><strong>Short answer.</strong> This is a documented fault, not
        something you did. AlphaTheta reported that an internal component defect
        in certain early units caused no audio output, display blackouts and
        system freezes, and firmware {XDJ_AZ.audioBlackoutFreezeFix} addresses
        the same symptom set. There is a free inspection and repair programme for
        affected units.</p>
        <p><strong>Why this happens.</strong> On a separate CDJ and mixer a
        single failure takes one deck out. On an all-in-one the decks, the mixer
        and the screen share one unit, so the same fault presents as the entire
        booth going silent or dark at once, which reads as catastrophic and is a
        known issue with a fix.</p>
        <p><strong>Fix it now.</strong> Update the firmware to the highest
        published version, currently {FLOOR}, which is the software half. For the
        hardware side, AlphaTheta did not publish a serial number range, so do not
        try to judge from the serial whether a unit is affected. Contact
        AlphaTheta support and ask about the inspection and repair programme by
        name. In the room tonight, if a unit is failing this way, the reliable
        move is a different unit or a linked player, because a hardware defect
        will not clear itself mid-set.</p>
        <p><strong>Avoid it next time.</strong> Check the firmware version on any
        AZ you are handed as part of setup, the same way you would check anything
        else, and if you own one from the first production run, run it through the
        programme before it lets you down at a gig rather than after.</p>
        <p class="acc-related">Related: <a href="#defect-notice">The inspection and repair notice</a> <a href="#firmware">Firmware, and what each version fixed</a> <a href="/knowledge/pioneer-dj/firmware">Every model, by firmware version</a></p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="acc-sec" name="xdjaz-acc" id="file-systems">
      <summary><h3 class="acc-h2">Which drives and formats it reads</h3><span class="acc-chev" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
      <div class="acc-body">
        <p><strong>Short answer.</strong> It reads <strong>{FS}</strong>, and NTFS
        is not supported. exFAT works here, which is the difference from older
        units that a DJ does not expect. Firmware updates specifically need a
        drive formatted FAT or FAT32.</p>
        <p><strong>Why this matters.</strong> A large drive formatted exFAT, which
        an older CDJ generation refuses, plays on this unit. NTFS, the Windows
        default for big drives, is refused everywhere in this range including
        here. On macOS the GUID Partition Map is not supported, and a Mac Extended
        case-sensitive volume may not read reliably, so the safe Mac option is
        HFS+ on the older partition scheme.</p>
        <p><strong>Fix it now.</strong> If a drive is refused, check the format
        before anything else. Only the first partition of a multi-partition drive
        is used, unless one partition holds a rekordbox library, in which case
        that one is used instead. A drive built around a flash card reader can
        fail regardless of format.</p>
        <p><strong>Avoid it next time.</strong> A single exFAT or FAT32 partition,
        exported from a current rekordbox so the OneLibrary trap above does not
        catch you as well. Keep a FAT or FAT32 stick for firmware updates, since
        those will not run from exFAT or HFS+.</p>
        <p class="acc-related">Related: <a href="#database-not-found">The database not found message</a> <a href="/fix/exfat-vs-fat32-cdj">exFAT or FAT32</a> <a href="/fix/format-usb-for-cdj">How to format a drive</a></p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <AccGroup icon="warn" title="Known issues" />

    <details class="acc-sec" name="xdjaz-acc" id="defect-notice">
      <summary><h3 class="acc-h2">The inspection and repair notice for early units</h3><span class="acc-chev" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
      <div class="acc-body">
        <p><strong>What it is.</strong> AlphaTheta published a notice that an
        internal component defect in certain units caused no audio output, display
        blackouts and system freezes, and offered a free inspection and repair for
        affected units. It concerns units from the first sales period.</p>
        <p><strong>What is documented and what is not.</strong> The symptoms and
        the offer of a free repair are documented. A serial number range is not,
        and no follow-up notice naming affected serials or confirming the
        programme is closed was published. So there is no way to read a serial and
        know, and this page will not invent a range.</p>
        <p><strong>What to do.</strong> If you own or rent an early AZ, contact
        AlphaTheta support and ask about the inspection and repair programme
        directly. Update to the highest published firmware regardless, since
        {XDJ_AZ.audioBlackoutFreezeFix} addresses the same symptom set in
        software.</p>
        <p class="acc-related">Related: <a href="#no-audio">No audio, blackouts or freezes</a> <a href={XDJ_AZ.sourceDefectNotice} rel="noopener">AlphaTheta's notice</a></p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="acc-sec" name="xdjaz-acc" id="recording-stop">
      <summary><h3 class="acc-h2">The recording will not stop</h3><span class="acc-chev" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
      <div class="acc-body">
        <p><strong>Short answer.</strong> An early firmware had a fault where
        pressing the Rec button during a recording did nothing and the recording
        could not be stopped. Firmware {XDJ_AZ.recStopFix} fixed it, so the
        answer is to update to the highest published version.</p>
        <p><strong>Why this matters.</strong> A recording that will not stop keeps
        writing to the drive, and the file grows until you find another way to end
        it. It is not a drive fault and reformatting is not the fix, it is
        firmware.</p>
        <p><strong>Fix it now.</strong> Update the firmware. If you are mid-set on
        an un-updated unit and the recording is stuck, ending the recording
        cleanly may mean stopping playback and letting the unit finish writing
        rather than pulling the drive, because a drive pulled while writing can
        lose the file.</p>
        <p class="acc-related">Related: <a href="#firmware">Firmware, and what each version fixed</a> <a href="#connections">Connections and recording</a></p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="acc-sec" name="xdjaz-acc" id="library-unresponsive">
      <summary><h3 class="acc-h2">A "Library is not responding" message keeps appearing</h3><span class="acc-chev" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
      <div class="acc-body">
        <p><strong>Short answer.</strong> A fault where that message kept
        appearing was fixed in firmware {XDJ_AZ.libraryUnresponsiveFix}. If you
        are seeing it, the unit is on older firmware and the fix is to update.</p>
        <p><strong>Why this matters.</strong> A library that reports itself
        unresponsive stops you browsing and loading, which on an all-in-one is the
        whole instrument. It is a known firmware fault with a published fix rather
        than a sign the drive or the library is damaged.</p>
        <p><strong>Fix it now.</strong> Update to the highest published version.
        In the room on an un-updated unit, reloading the drive or switching to a
        different prepared drive is the workaround while the message persists.</p>
        <p class="acc-related">Related: <a href="#firmware">Firmware, and what each version fixed</a> <a href="#database-not-found">The database not found message</a></p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <AccGroup icon="sliders" title="Features explained" />

    <details class="acc-sec" name="xdjaz-acc" id="features">
      <summary><h3 class="acc-h2">What the AZ is, and how it is laid out</h3><span class="acc-chev" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
      <div class="acc-body">
        <p><strong>The shape of it.</strong> Four channels, four decks of onboard
        playback, a {XDJ_AZ.screen}, two top-loading USB ports and one USB Type-C
        to a computer. It is a whole booth in one unit, built to feel like a pair
        of CDJs beside a DJM rather than like a controller.</p>
        <p><strong>Software.</strong> It runs standalone from a drive with no
        computer, and it also unlocks rekordbox performance mode and Serato DJ Pro
        for free when connected to a laptop over USB, with Serato support added in
        firmware {XDJ_AZ.seratoFrom}. Streaming play from services was added
        across later firmware.</p>
        <p><strong>What it is not.</strong> It has no send and return loop for an
        outboard effector, which the older XDJ-XZ does have. If your set depends on
        patching an external effects unit into the mixer, that is a booking-stage
        fact about this model.</p>
        <p class="acc-related">Related: <a href="#connections">Connections and recording</a> <a href="#compatibility">What it works with</a></p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <AccGroup icon="usb" title="Connections" />

    <details class="acc-sec" name="xdjaz-acc" id="connections">
      <summary><h3 class="acc-h2">Connections, and recording</h3><span class="acc-chev" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
      <div class="acc-body">
        <p><strong>Inputs.</strong> {XDJ_AZ.micInputs} mic inputs on XLR or TRS,
        and {XDJ_AZ.phonoInputs} switchable LINE or PHONO inputs on RCA with a
        ground terminal, so a pair of turntables goes straight in. There is no
        dedicated send and return.</p>
        <p><strong>Outputs and computer.</strong> Balanced XLR and RCA master,
        a TRS booth, two headphone jacks, a LAN port for PRO DJ LINK, and a USB
        Type-C to a computer. Windows needs the AZ audio driver, macOS uses its
        own, so the unit doubles as the soundcard for rekordbox or Serato.</p>
        <p><strong>Recording.</strong> It records to a connected USB drive. Master
        level and master EQ do not change what is recorded, and there is a cap on
        the number of files in the recording folder, so clear old recordings off a
        drive you plan to record onto.</p>
        <p class="acc-related">Related: <a href="#recording-stop">The recording will not stop</a> <a href="#compatibility">What it works with</a></p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <AccGroup icon="sync" title="Compatibility" />

    <details class="acc-sec" name="xdjaz-acc" id="compatibility">
      <summary><h3 class="acc-h2">What it works with, and linking more players</h3><span class="acc-chev" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
      <div class="acc-body">
        <p><strong>Library and software.</strong> rekordbox for Mac, Windows, iOS
        and Android in export and link modes, rekordbox performance mode unlocked
        over USB, and Serato DJ Pro unlocked over USB. Read the drive from a
        current rekordbox so it carries OneLibrary, per the emergency section
        above.</p>
        <p><strong>DVS.</strong> It supports DVS through rekordbox and through
        Serato, licences separate, using the two LINE or PHONO inputs and a pair
        of turntables. Timecode brings its own failure a pressed record does not:
        a worn control record degrades tracking before it sounds obviously bad.</p>
        <p><strong>Linking more players.</strong> It is PRO DJ LINK compatible, so
        CDJs join the setup over a LAN cable and a drive in any linked unit is
        browsable from the others. That link is also where the E-8302 family of
        errors appears, exactly as on a CDJ booth.</p>
        <p class="acc-related">Related: <a href="/fix/cdj-error-e-8302">CDJ error E-8302</a> <a href="/knowledge/pioneer-dj/rekordbox">The rekordbox reference</a></p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <AccGroup icon="book" title="Understanding the unit" />

    <details class="acc-sec" name="xdjaz-acc" id="firmware">
      <summary><h3 class="acc-h2">Firmware, and what each version fixed</h3><span class="acc-chev" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
      <div class="acc-body">
        <p><strong>The fixes that matter.</strong> Firmware
        {XDJ_AZ.recStopFix} fixed a recording that could not be stopped.
        {XDJ_AZ.audioBlackoutFreezeFix} addressed no audio, display blackouts and
        system freezes on some units. {XDJ_AZ.seratoFrom} added Serato DJ Pro.
        {XDJ_AZ.libraryUnresponsiveFix} fixed a library that kept reporting itself
        unresponsive. Highest published version is {FLOOR}.</p>
        <p><strong>Reading it in the booth.</strong> The full model to version
        table lives on the firmware reference, so you can read the version off the
        unit and see which documented faults are still live on it.</p>
        <p><strong>Standby.</strong> Power management ships enabled with a
        {XDJ_AZ.standbyMinutesDefault} minute default, which powers the unit down
        after that long with no activity. A unit that switched itself off during a
        long changeover is obeying that setting.</p>
        <p class="acc-related">Related: <a href="/knowledge/pioneer-dj/firmware">Every model, by firmware version</a> <a href={XDJ_AZ.sourceFirmware} rel="noopener">AlphaTheta firmware page</a></p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="acc-sec" name="xdjaz-acc" id="specs">
      <summary><h3 class="acc-h2">The reference numbers</h3><span class="acc-chev" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
      <div class="acc-body">
        <p><strong>The published figures.</strong> {XDJ_AZ.channels} channels,
        {XDJ_AZ.decks} decks, a {XDJ_AZ.screen}. {XDJ_AZ.dimensions}, weight
        {XDJ_AZ.weight}. Announced {XDJ_AZ.announced}. Model names:
        {XDJ_AZ.variants}.</p>
        <p><strong>Lineage.</strong> AlphaTheta name the {XDJ_AZ.predecessorNamed}
        as its predecessor, and describe the AZ as an evolution of it. Both are
        covered here.</p>
        <p class="acc-related">Related: <a href="/knowledge/pioneer-dj/xdj-xz">The XDJ-XZ</a> <a href={XDJ_AZ.source} rel="noopener">AlphaTheta product page</a></p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <RelatedEquipment slug="xdj-az" />

    <EmailCapture source="knowledge_xdj_az" />
  </main>
</Base>

